# Skill Output Structure

When a skill produces deliverables worth keeping (audits, plans, checklists, step summaries), write them under `.cursor/skill-outputs/` — never scatter skill artifacts in source trees.

## Path layout

```text
.cursor/skill-outputs/
  {feature}/
    {layer}/
      {timestamp}_{skill-name}/
        {NN}_{step-slug}.md
```

| Segment | Format | Example |
|---------|--------|---------|
| `feature` | kebab-case product area | `editor`, `export`, `onboarding` |
| `layer` | kebab-case layer from [pixelanea-agent-tools.mdc](./pixelanea-agent-tools.mdc) | `canvas`, `domain`, `api` |
| `timestamp` | `YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS` (UTC, sortable) | `20260731T054200` |
| `skill-name` | kebab-case; basename of the skill folder | `pixelanea-frontend-standards` |
| `step` | `{NN}_{step-slug}.md` — zero-padded, 2+ digits | `01_audit-tool-context.md` |

## Example

```text
.cursor/skill-outputs/
  editor/
    canvas/
      20260731T054200_pixelanea-frontend-standards/
        01_audit-tool-context.md
        02_refactor-input-routing.md
    domain/
      20260731T061500_pixelanea-cpp-standards/
        01_review-frame-model.md
```

## Step file contents

Each `{NN}_{step-slug}.md` should be self-contained:

1. **Goal** — what this step set out to do (one sentence).
2. **Outcome** — decisions, findings, or changes produced.
3. **Files** — paths touched or reviewed (if any).

Keep steps atomic: one concern per file; add `02_`, `03_`, … for later steps in the same run.

## When to write

- **Do** persist outputs when the skill spans multiple steps or the user may revisit the work.
- **Do** create the full directory chain before writing the first step file.
- **Don't** write here for trivial one-line answers or pure in-chat explanations.
- **Don't** duplicate source code — link paths and summarize instead.
